rcise plays a fundamental role in promoting muscle growth and overall physical fitness.\",5\r\n1782,DIETA ORAL,\"DIETA ORAL refers to the normal diet that most patients transition to after undergoing metabolic surgery, although some individuals may encounter complications that hinder this process. It is recognized as the preferred method of nutritional support for hospitalized patients, as it aims to fulfill their energy and nutrient requirements through food intake. Additionally, an oral diet is essential for patients with liver diseases, helping them maintain adequate nutrition. However, it is important to note that the intake of food and drink by mouth can also trigger the onset of ascitis quilosa in certain patients. Overall, DIETA ORAL encompasses the dietary practices that are vital for recovery and health maintenance in various patient populations.\",7\r\n1791,ENFERMEDADES ASOCIADAS,Associated diseases that may increase the risk of malnutrition and require special dietary considerations for hospitalized patients.,1\r\n1792,PACIENTE HOSPITALIZADO,,1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n3486,PACIENTE,MICRONUTRIENTES,Los pacientes trasplantados deben recibir una cantidad adecuada de micronutrientes para apoyar su recuperación,564\r\n3491,PACIENTE,REQUERIMIENTOS NUTRICIONALES,Los requerimientos nutricionales del paciente determinan el tipo de fórmula y régimen de nutrición enteral que se le debe administrar.,553\r\n4730,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,MICRONUTRIENTES,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL involves the careful management of MICRONUTRIENTES to ensure that patients receive the necessary nutrients without experiencing deficiencies or excesses. It is crucial to monitor micronutrient levels closely in parenteral nutrition, as these nutrients are essential for maintaining health. The inclusion of micronutrients in parenteral nutrition is aimed at preventing deficiencies in patients who rely on this method of nutrition. Ove